2026-10-21T04:33:51.0274710Z To enable PHP in Apache add the following to httpd.conf and restart Apache:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0275400Z     LoadModule php_module /opt/homebrew/opt/php@8.4/lib/httpd/modules/libphp.so
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0277500Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0277590Z     <FilesMatch \.php$>
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0277820Z         SetHandler application/x-httpd-php
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0278180Z     </FilesMatch>
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0278280Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0278460Z Finally, check DirectoryIndex includes index.php
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0278740Z     DirectoryIndex index.php index.html
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0278900Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0279070Z The php.ini and php-fpm.ini file can be found in:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0279340Z     /opt/homebrew/etc/php/8.4/
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0279470Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0279610Z To start php@8.4 now and restart at login:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0279830Z   brew services start php@8.4
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0280180Z Or, if you don't want/need a background service you can just run:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0280530Z   /opt/homebrew/opt/php@8.4/sbin/php-fpm --nodaemonize
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0280870Z [34m==>[0m [1mllvm[0m
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0281160Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR: /opt/homebrew/etc/clang
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0281480Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_USER_DIR:   ~/.config/clang
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0281640Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0281810Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0282050Z   brew install lld
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0282210Z   brew install lldb
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0282310Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0282570Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0283000Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0283180Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0283530Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0284180Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0284540Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0284650Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0284870Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0285220Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0285410Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0285600Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0286260Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0286980Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0287520Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0287850Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0288000Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0288370Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0288690Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0288920Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0289410Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0289790Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0289940Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0290090Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0290500Z   echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:$PATH"' >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0290760Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0290920Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0291220Z   export LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib"
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0291520Z   export CPPFLAGS="-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include"
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0291690Z 
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0291830Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-21T04:33:51.0292110Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm"
